 ('4:20-4:24 | Explain the checks', 'say', "So far, we've used made-up information. Working with real applications brings a different responsibility. People have trusted us with details about their lives.\n\nBefore using a tool, we need to know whether our organization has approved it for that information. Who can see what we enter? How long is it kept? Can it be deleted? What happens if something goes wrong? Removing a name may not be enough if the rest of the story still identifies the person.\n\nYou don't have to answer every technology question yourself. You do need to know who can help you answer it. Until the people responsible for privacy and the service have approved the use, keep practicing with made-up examples.\n\nWe also need to name who checks the output and who owns the final decision. 'Someone will check it' is easy to say and easy to miss."),
